  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 73ff519377b990a4c81cd1461a3c1f62, type: 3}
  m_Name: Tomas_W36_Teach
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueNode
  speakerName: Tomas
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 21300000, guid: ba6dfb4f62658bd4f9bcd95d048fa112, type: 3}
  dialogueText: 'No kayatmo a sumurot kenka ti maysa a tao, mabalinmo nga ibaga kenkuana
    nga sumurot.


    Iti Ilokano, ti ''surotennak'' ket kayatna a saoen ti ''follow
    me.''


    Usarem daytoy no mangidalan ka iti maysa a tao iti sabali a lugar.


    Denggem
    a naimbag: surotennak.


    Ita, padasem nga ibagam ti ''surotennak'' iti bukodmo
    a timek.'
  translatedText: 'When you want someone to come along with you, you can tell them
    to follow.

    In Ilokano, ''surotennak'' means ''follow me.''

    Use it when
    leading someone to another place.

    Now, try saying ''surotennak'' yourself.'
